From b7fe22c0755db263b6894fe6720792a31983af23 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: telegdyd <telegdyd93@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 14:33:47 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] jasmine-j0021: USB Ethernet (CDC-NCM) and a live log server
 on jasmine

sweet's DWC3 gadget (bsd/dev/sweet_usb.c) on jasmine: addresses and GCC
offsets from ADT /sweet-usb, whose presence also enables it there. The
function is CDC-NCM instead of CDC-ECM (Windows has an inbox driver only
for NCM): IAD + NCM descriptors, the NCM class requests, NTH16/NDP16 on
both bulk endpoints, speed-change then connection notifications. ue0 gets
192.168.7.2/24 and 169.254.7.2/16. The console log is served over TCP on
port 5140 (whole ring, then live) instead of pushed over UDP.
